pair(S, 'bit', 'What is a bit?', 'The smallest unit of binary data can hold which values?', 'One binary digit: 0 or 1', ['A group of eight characters', 'Any number from 0 to 255', 'A complete processor instruction'], 'A bit stores one binary digit.');
pair(S, 'byte', 'How many bits are in one byte?', 'A byte-sized power-up has how many binary digits?', '8', ['2', '16', '256'], 'One byte contains eight bits.');
pair(S, 'ascii', 'How many different codes can 8-bit extended ASCII represent?', 'An 8-bit extended ASCII character code has how many possible bit patterns?', '256', ['8', '128', '1000'], 'Eight bits give 2 to the power of 8, or 256 possible codes.');
pair(S, 'character-code', 'How is a character represented using extended ASCII?', 'The letter A appears in a player name. How can the computer represent it?', 'Using a binary code assigned to that character', ['By storing its outline as a vector', 'By storing the whole alphabet for each letter', 'Using a different processor for each character'], 'A character encoding assigns each character a numeric code stored in binary.');
