pair(S, 'vector-attributes', 'Which pair of attributes describes a vector rectangle?', 'You want to move and recolour a vector shape. Which attributes would you edit?', 'Coordinates and fill colour', ['Password and primary key', 'Pixel count and character code', 'Mantissa and exponent'], 'Coordinates position the object, and fill colour describes its interior.');
pair(S, 'vector-scale', 'What is an advantage of vector graphics when changing image size?', 'You enlarge a vector badge for the arcade wall. What happens to its edges?', 'They remain sharp because the objects are recalculated', ['They must become blocky at any larger size', 'They are converted into ASCII characters', 'The image loses all its colour'], 'Vector objects can be recalculated at a new size without pixelation.');
pair(S, 'mantissa', 'In floating point representation, what does the mantissa store?', 'A positive real number uses a mantissa and exponent. Which part stores its significant digits?', 'The significant digits of the number', ['The memory address', 'The character encoding', 'The number of processor registers'], 'The mantissa holds the significant digits; the exponent determines their scale.');
